  "source_attribution": [],
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "text": "Myntra has started using AI-generated product images for clothing listings, and it’s becoming difficult to trust what the actual product looks like. For a platform known for fashion shopping, real product photos should be the standard.",
      "source": "Play Store",
      "source_id": "c17ee023-5e35-4e55-8623-e51ea357deef",
      "date": "2026-08-15",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "tags": [
        "visual_trust"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the photos, the clothes look like they are of good quality, but when you receive them as a customer, you receive footpath quality stitching. I always make sure to check photos uploaded by reviewers to see the real colour and quality then.",
      "source": "YouTube",
      "source_id": "UgxL5BMpnYSYLdDJik94AaABAg",
      "date": "2023-11-20",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "tags": [
        "fabric_durability"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "I purchased converse chunk shoes on 21st July. The shoes are starting to come apart—is this the kind of quality you provide? Within just 20 days, the shoes have started separating at the sides. I bought shoes worth 4,000.",
      "source": "PissedConsumer",
      "source_id": "pc_p7_1600411",
      "date": "2026-08-17",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "tags": [
        "product_durability"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "They have no filter to check customer images. I was recently scrolling through ultimate glam clan and a lot of pictures there were obviously AI and not an ounce of authenticity.",
      "source": "Reddit",
      "source_id": "reddit_t3_1ukask8",
      "date": "2026-07-01",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "tags": [
        "aesthetic_feed_authenticity"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "In online there is no scope to try, so basically you have to take few more pieces than you wanted and whatever don't look good on you, you have to return..but Myntra took convience fees for those extra return..so, had to stop buying from Myntra..",
      "source": "YouTube",
      "source_id": "UgwYb-BW0jI6I4C0hYx4AaABAg",
      "date": "2023-11-07",
      "confidence": 0.89,
      "tags": [
        "value_for_money"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    }
  ],
